{"_v":1,"id":"crybaby-2008","cs":54,"rc":7,"bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":3,"negative":3},"rv":[{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/714601999/","d":"2008-04-25","q":"It's pretty stupid, yes, but with brains."},{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2008/04/24/AR2008042403189.html","d":"2008-04-25","q":"The musical 'Cry-Baby,' which opened Thursday night at the Marquis Theatre, is a moderately entertaining exercise in camp that never quite decides what it wants to be when it grows up."},{"cn":"Chris Jones","o":"Chicago Tribune","s":49,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/234559709/","d":"2008-04-27","q":"Albeit with some decent laughs, a certain sense of fun and a few redeeming scenes and performances, \""},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":45,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2008/legit/reviews/cry-baby-1200472551/","d":"2008-04-24","q":"But without a central romance that cooks, the show’s pleasures evaporate as they unfold."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":37,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2008/04/25/theater/reviews/25cryb.html","d":"2008-04-25","q":"This show in search of an identity has all the saliva-stirring properties of week-old pre-chewed gum."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":55,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"http://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/CryBaby.html","d":"2008-04-25","q":"On the most basic of terms, Cry"},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/cry-baby/","d":"2008-05-16","q":"Although consistently entertaining in a trashy bubble gum kind of way “Cry Baby” with its bright colorful design feels like a pale imitation of “Hairspray” without a hint of danger or the political ramifications of the predecessor."}],"au":{"score":53,"designation":"Disliking","sources":